{"step_index":263,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:30:57Z","input_tokens":2637,"cache_read_tokens":186885,"output_tokens":425,"content":"### Why Gemini Was Able to Read the Answers\nIn the previous build, a fallback `defaultQuiz` object containing the 20 questions, answer keys, and explanations was included inside `index.html` as an offline safety measure. Because that data was written directly in the static source code, anyone opening the file or feeding it to an AI could immediately view all 20 answers.\n\n### Proposed Fix\nCompletely remove `defaultQuiz` and all hardcoded questions/answers from [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html):\n1. **0 Hardcoded Questions/Answers**: The source code of `index.html` will contain **zero questions, zero answer keys, and zero explanations**.\n2. **Strict Dynamic Loading**: The student client will solely query Firebase Firestore at runtime. The \"Start Quiz\" button will remain disabled until questions are securely fetched over the network.\n3. **AI & View-Source Protected**: Feeding `index.html` to Gemini, ChatGPT, or viewing page source will reveal no quiz content.\n\nI have updated the plan in [implementation_plan.md](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/implementation_plan.md).\n\nMay I have your approval to remove all hardcoded quiz data from [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)? (You can reply directly in text or click the Proceed button on the implementation plan artifact)."}
