{"step_index":308,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:46:38Z","input_tokens":3377,"cache_read_tokens":214073,"output_tokens":549,"content":"I tested your updated security rules against the live Firestore database and confirmed:\n1. **Reading `/quizzes/{quizId}`** works with `status: 200` (allowed).\n2. **Submissions (`/quizzes/{quizId}/submissions`)** works with `status: 200` as long as the document strictly conforms to the 11 keys (`['n','s','raw','sw','pen','sc','tot','ts','t','code','submittedAt']`) and name/section length is $< 100$.\n3. **Writing `/quizzes/{quizId}`** returns `403 PERMISSION_DENIED` because `allow write: if false;` prevents all browser-side writes to the quiz document.\n\n### Required Compatibility Updates:\n1. **[index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)**:\n   - Add `maxlength=\"99\"` to the Name (`#nm`) and Section (`#sc`) inputs so users cannot enter $\\ge 100$ characters.\n   - Sanitize the submission payload so it contains **strictly and only** the 11 allowed keys, with strings sliced to `< 100` characters, ensuring Firestore never rejects a valid student submission.\n2. **[teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)**:\n   - Update error feedback when clicking \"Save to Quiz\" so that if `403 PERMISSION_DENIED` occurs, it clearly explains that `/quizzes/{quizId}` is currently locked by Firestore security rules.\n   - Add a \"Download Quiz JSON\" button as an offline backup for the teacher.\n\nPlease review the detailed plan in [implementation_plan.md](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/implementation_plan.md).\n\nMay I have your approval to implement these compatibility updates? (You can reply directly in text or click the Proceed button on the implementation plan artifact)."}
